title: Kubernetes: Monitoring agent node-scraper health
agents: kubernetes
catalog: containerization/kubernetes
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This optional cluster-host service checks one node's kubelet statistics,
 kubelet health and system-agent payloads independently. Receipt age is {WARN}
 at 90 seconds and {CRIT} at 120 seconds. An expected payload that is missing
 from the cache is {CRIT}. These states have no startup grace period.

 The service reports the receipt age of each payload independently. Scrape
 durations, node-scraper versions and Git revisions are available in the
 service details and metrics.

 Missing cached data may never have arrived or may have expired. The defaults
 accommodate a 60-second collection interval and 120-second cache retention.
 After expiry the missing-payload state takes precedence over age thresholds.

 The rule {Kubernetes agent node health} configures receipt-age thresholds,
 missing-payload state, and version mismatch state ({OK} by default).
 Item conditions allow different settings for different nodes. Version and
 Git revision are shown per payload. Missing optional metadata is informational.
 Each payload with available measurements has receipt-age and scrape-duration
 metrics. Disabling age thresholds does not disable missing-data detection.

 The cluster overview continues to evaluate the node independently using its
 own rule. Both services can alert for the same fault. Nodes removed from the
 section use the standard vanished-service behavior.

item:
 Kubernetes node name.
discovery:
 One service per reported node-scraper node when node services are enabled
 in {Kubernetes agent health service discovery}. Also discovers nodes whose
 payloads are absent from the cache. Services reside on the cluster host.
